# TERM SHEET — SERIES A PREFERRED SHARE FINANCING

**Company:** GreenGrid Analytics Ltd ("the Company")
**Round:** Series A
**Lead Investor:** Northbridge Ventures LLP
**Date:** 2 May 2026

This term sheet summarises the principal terms proposed for a Series A Preferred Share financing of GreenGrid Analytics Ltd. It is non-binding except for the Confidentiality, Governing Law, and Exclusivity provisions below.

## 1. The Financing

| Term | Detail |
|---|---|
| Amount Raised | £3,200,000 |
| Pre-Money Valuation | £12,000,000 |
| Post-Money Valuation | £15,200,000 |
| Price Per Share | £1.50 |
| New Shares Issued | 2,133,333 Series A Preferred Shares |
| Existing Ordinary Shares (pre-round) | 8,000,000 |
| Fully Diluted Shares (post-round) | 10,133,333 |
| Investor Ownership (post-round) | 21.05% |

## 2. Liquidation Preference

1x non-participating liquidation preference. In a liquidity event, Series A holders receive the greater of (a) their original investment amount, or (b) the amount they would receive on an as-converted basis.

## 3. Anti-Dilution

Broad-based weighted average anti-dilution protection.

## 4. Board Composition

The Board shall consist of three (3) directors: two (2) appointed by the holders of Ordinary Shares (the founders), and one (1) appointed by the holders of Series A Preferred Shares.

## 5. Protective Provisions

Standard protective provisions requiring Series A investor consent for: (a) any amendment to the Articles of Association adverse to Series A holders, (b) any sale of the Company, (c) any new class of shares senior to or pari passu with Series A, (d) incurrence of debt above £250,000 outside the ordinary course.

## 6. Information Rights

Investors holding at least 2% of fully diluted share capital are entitled to quarterly management accounts and an annual budget.

## 7. Conditions to Closing

Satisfactory completion of legal, financial, and technical due diligence per the Company's standard due-diligence checklist; delivery of a clean disclosure letter; execution of an Investment Agreement, Amended Articles of Association, and Shareholders' Agreement.

## 8. Confidentiality & Exclusivity

The Company agrees to a 45-day exclusivity period from the date of this term sheet during which it will not solicit or negotiate alternative financing proposals.

